    "postalCode": {
      "label": "NNNNN (department/region + routing zone + postal district/locality)",
      "required": true,
      "usage": "Use only an exact, time-bound MTC Código Postal Nacional observation or a release-pinned official row. The first two digits identify the department or postal region, the third identifies a road-network routing zone, and the final two identify a postal district, locality, populated centre or urban concentration; valid syntax alone is not current assignment evidence. The 2018 open XLSX can support dated assignments only with its exact ODC Attribution licence snapshot, release date, schema and digest, and it is not a polygon release. The official lookup labels geographic boundaries as referential, so a lookup result, map rendering, Ubigeo, IGN or GeoVivienda boundary, COFOPRI parcel or construction, community object, buffer, interpolation, Voronoi surface or model output is not official MTC postcode geometry. A service-area polygon may be derived for review only from exact, rights-cleared, time-compatible assignment, routing and locality evidence with uncertainty and unmatched coverage explicit. Never infer a street, number, block, lot, unit, person, owner, occupant or exact building from postcode containment. Building display requires a rights-cleared stable civic-address identifier and an explicit reviewed relation to a permitted construction identifier. AGID remains an independent versioned spatial crosswalk."
    },
